<title>SPAIN: Spain's INE revises calendar adj Dec indust output.</title>
<headline>Spain's INE revises calendar adj Dec indust output.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's December calendar-adjusted industrial production has been revised to a fall of 2.2 percent versus an originally announced fall of 2.1 percent, National Statistics Institute INE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown of calendar-adjusted figures, which take into account differences in the number of working days (percentage change year on year):</p>
<p>					   JAN 97	DEC 96</p>
<p> General index			  5.1	   -2.2R</p>
<p> Consumption goods		    8.2	   -2.6</p>
<p> Capital goods			  9.7	   -2.5R</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   1.9	   -2.0R</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
